  The paper's V_ISO1/V_EFE1 columns are the n=1 interpolation function, which IS this repository's Route A kernel;
  item 46 reproduced them to 2%, so the scaling a_0 ~ (V_obs/V_pred)^4 used here is the paper's own calculation.
  Caveat the paper itself raises and item 46 booked: these discs have completed under one orbit since the merger,
  so dynamical equilibrium is not established.  That is why rung D is quoted and not used.
    RUNG  D  Lelli+2015 tidal dwarfs (EFE included)    a_0 = 1.734e-11  +- 0.170 dex   (-0.73 canon, -0.81 alt)   6 objects, 3 independent hosts; equilibrium not established
  [PASS] 124.D AGAINST INTEREST: tidal debris, the cleanest stellar-mass-free system there is in principle, gives an a_0 a factor 3-6 below both footings on the published kinematics.  This is item 46's liability restated as a number for the ladder.  It is not a kill (one orbit since the merger) but it is not evidence either way for a_0, and it cannot be quietly left out of a stellar-mass-free ladder   (a_0(TDG, EFE) = 1.734e-11 +- 0.081 dex, -0.73 dex from canonical, -0.81 from alt)

